l;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T23:48:31-07:00","id":967797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/966791-can-i-get-a-changeling-with-retinue?p=966952#post966952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">meant can I get a changeling as a Retainer... its Easy to picture those with high degrees of title but seems to work against the letter and spirit of the background and im being put on the spot on the issue right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Retinue replaces Retainer, as per the description above. The character could take Chimera (Chimerical Companion) to get a retainer, instead or as well. <br /> <br /> I'd just direct them to Retinue. Retainer doesn't usually cover Enchanted beings, so the player would have the problem of their staff constantly forgetting who they are every time the Mists kick in. Retinue solves that problem, as the humans are explicitly Enchanted or affected by magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-12-2016, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","ava